Fillets: the piece ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd cuts on the spine's end edge,
before the rest of that edge's analytic blend, runs on that blend's
surface where it is the same, so the two are one face, as patch 1352 does
for the piece past the end (mitcad#1422).

The plate's top edge rounded as a tangent chain up to a boss: picked at
one side, the blend along each side is one cylinder face; picked at the
other, the walk's pieces were split so that the face at the end cut them
(ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd), and each side's blend was two faces of one
cylinder, named as numbered pieces where the result of the other pick has
one face. Now the result has the same faces whichever edge is picked.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_boss_tangent.cpp, the plate's top edge
picked at its other side: the rounding of that edge one face named after
it.

Upstream: new.

